+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers considering a change to pickup reminders, including switching to email to save the SMS cost.
+Pickup reminders go by SMS because an email trial increased missed pickups and wasted fresh food. Repeated
+proposals to switch prompted this explanation; [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md) records the trial and the decision
+to keep SMS.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+From April to June 2025, larder tried email reminders. The provider reported that 34% of reminder emails were never
+opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders. Each missed pickup leaves a packed bag whose fresh
+food goes in the bin by closing time. The pantry lead reported that many members share one phone in the family and
+never check email, but do see SMS.
+
+Larder switched back to SMS on July 1, 2025; by August, missed pickups were back to 6%. In issue 52, a volunteer
+proposed email again to save the reported €40 monthly SMS cost. The maintainer kept SMS: reaching members and
+avoiding missed pickups and food waste outweigh that saving.
+
+## Implementation
+
+The reminder channel and sending behavior live in [`larder/reminders.py`](../../larder/reminders.py).
